  "body": "Adds **Security Lab** to the browser toolbar. Run Test verifies a fresh local session is denied, evaluates deterministic AegisMock Allow, checks protected fixture access, confirms another session remains denied, then verifies reset revocation. Passed requires all nine assertions. Open Test Page uses the existing tab lifecycle with a separate in-memory request context. The UI shows status, decision/request ID and exports a sanitized assertion report.\n\nASP.NET Core Kestrel binds only to 127.0.0.1 on an automatically assigned port. Cryptographically random session IDs map to server-side grants; forged `decision=allow` values cannot authorize. Errors, invalid results and reset revoke grants. No real providers, credentials, external detection calls or security bypasses. Existing Smart Search, profiles, privacy and Chromium protections are retained.\n\n[Windows run 39970819828](https://github.com/roshan-pandit1/AegisBrowser/actions/runs/39970819828) passed for implementation 7b662472: 26 mock Allow, 56 privacy, 49 search, 50 policy/profile and 49 native browser write checks; 8 storage checks in each of three read processes; 20 Chromium filtering checks; 3+4 settings restart checks. Restore/build/publish and existing TLS/popup/renderer/shutdown regressions passed. Portable extraction verified 852 file hashes and extracted-app startup/normal-close smoke.\n\n[Windows x64 portable test artifact](https://github.com/roshan-pandit1/AegisBrowser/actions/runs/39970819828/artifacts/12508009706). Includes installation and SECURITY-LAB-MOCK-ALLOW instructions. BUILD-STATUS.md records the route-serialization and context-test defects corrected during verification.\n\nManual UI acceptance is **NOT RUN**. Remaining: keyboard/scaling, repeated-run and report/export UX, page-button/reset UX, closing during active work and normal browsing with lab tabs. The runner and fixture page use separate sessions; Run Test ends by revoking its own session. Keep draft and do not merge automatically. This branch starts from main and is independent of draft PR #6.\n\nFinal branch verification: [Windows CI 39971483169](https://github.com/roshan-pandit1/AegisBrowser/actions/runs/39971483169) PASSED on 4a0124cb, including BUILD-STATUS.md. Completed logs confirm all test counts above and 852-file portable verification. [Latest portable Windows x64 test artifact](https://github.com/roshan-pandit1/AegisBrowser/actions/runs/39971483169/artifacts/12509990722). Inner ZIP SHA-256: `35e94995094b74d8067eee5c47bd358d0f4905fab94698f714976f0599494ca2`.",
